{"parentUuid":"6fa259f6-38b8-4a1b-8556-1924ee9cd8c2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7880d82c-265a-4bca-a786-f6cb7147359f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H69sfK2iY9otfMbgueNPAA","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"space\": \"01f1a9dab08014b2a9c9b627aa714843\", \"conversation\": \"01f1a9db240d1a7d8e28a6fb2f6a279e\", \"has_sql\": true, \"rows\": 2, \"event\": \"genie.answer\", \"level\": \"info\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-06T10:10:29.173463Z\"}\r\nconfigured: True | space: 01f1a9dab08014b2a9c9b627aa714843 | reason: None\r\nTEXT: You want to see which features experienced regressions and the extent of those regressions in terms of percentage change and severity.The **discounts** feature regressed twice, with severity levels of **MEDIUM** and **LOW**. The regression amounts were **11.9%** and **4.26%** respectively. Both regressions affected the same feature but with different severity and impact.\r\nSQL: SELECT v.`feature`, r.`change_percent`, v.`regression_severity` FROM `workspace`.`devmemory`.`fact_versions` v INNER JOIN `workspace`.`devmemory`.`fact_regressions` r ON v.`project_id` = r.`project_id` AND v.`version_id` = r.`version_id` WHERE v.`status` = 'REGRESSION' AND v.`feature` IS NOT NULL AND r.`change_percent` IS NOT NULL AND v.`regression_severity` IS NOT NULL\r\nCOLUMNS: ['feature', 'change_percent', 'regression_severity']\r\nROWS: [['discounts', '11.9', 'MEDIUM'], ['discounts', '4.26', 'LOW']]\r\nconversation_id: 01f1a9db240d1a7d8e28a6fb2f6a279e","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"10ae2c29-b629-43dd-9782-a48f764ef4b3","timestamp":"2026-09-06T10:10:29.393Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6fa259f6-38b8-4a1b-8556-1924ee9cd8c2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing