{"parentUuid":"5d6081a3-8cc6-4baf-8137-e9f288d1ad56","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen1KZgbTTDcpnqBNQJi9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"✅ **It's live and working.** I set the space ID in `/tmp/tl-demo/.devmemory/config.json` and tested the full path — Genie answered \"Which features regressed and by how much?\" with text, a result table (`discounts → 8.08%` avg), and the real SQL against `workspace.devmemory.fact_versions/fact_regressions`. Follow-up questions keep the conversation context. Screenshot confirms the UI renders all of it.\n\n**To run it yourself:**\n```powershell\n$env:DATABRICKS_HOST         = \"https://dbc-1b5e869b-0d1a.cloud.databricks.com\"\n$env:DATABRICKS_TOKEN        = \"REDACTED\"\n$env:DATABRICKS_WAREHOUSE_ID = \"9d0fe00fe4756c71\"\ncd C:\\Users\\BANU\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\tl-demo\ndevmemory serve\n```\nThe space ID is already in the config file, so no `DATABRICKS_GENIE_SPACE_ID` needed for this project. Dashboard → **Ask**.\n\nWhat changed in that config: `catalog: \"workspace\"`, `schema: \"devmemory\"`, `enabled: true`, `genie_space_id: \"01f1a9dab08014b2a9c9b627aa714843\"`.\n\nNothing new to commit — the feature code was already in `446a2f3`. Reminder still stands: rotate that Databricks token (and the OpenAI/Gemini keys) after the hackathon since they're in this transcript."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":544,"cache_read_input_tokens":286238,"output_tokens":533,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":544,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":533,"cache_read_input_tokens":286238,"cache_creation_input_tokens":544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_token