{"parentUuid":"25bd5892-ed25-4e03-b2f9-45e75480ffe8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen23w2ewW5HpPa19jZuy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The global `devmemory-cli` on PyPI is still **`0.1.0.dev0`** — built before the Genie feature, so it doesn't know the `genie_space_id` config key (and has no Genie chat at all). Your shell isn't in the `.venv` anymore, so `python -m devmemory` is hitting that old install.\n\n**Fastest — use the source build** (this is what worked in testing):\n\n```powershell\nD:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\ncd C:\\Users\\BANU\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\tl-demo\n$env:DATABRICKS_HOST         = \"https://dbc-1b5e869b-0d1a.cloud.databricks.com\"\n$env:DATABRICKS_TOKEN        = \"REDACTED\"\n$env:DATABRICKS_WAREHOUSE_ID = \"9d0fe00fe4756c71\"\ndevmemory serve\n```\n\n(The space ID is already in `tl-demo`'s config.json.)\n\n**Or publish dev1 and upgrade the global install:**\n```powershell\ncd D:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek\npython -m twine upload --username __token__ --password \"pypi-<NEW-TOKEN>\" dist/devmemory_cli-0.1.0.dev1*\npip install --pre --upgrade devmemory-cli\n```\n`dist/` already has the dev1 artifacts built and checked."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1786,"cache_read_input_tokens":293219,"output_tokens":1000,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":503},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1786,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":293219,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1786},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ce