{"parentUuid":"c1bd93c2-888c-4c89-855f-60ee2735b3ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen2F92XVMcZgiLRxgZ2U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`pip` still shows `0.1.0.dev0` — **the dev1 upload never went through** (PyPI still only has dev0). So `--upgrade` had nothing newer to fetch.\n\nSkip the global package for now — **run the source build directly** (full path, no venv activation needed):\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\BANU\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\tl-demo\n$env:DATABRICKS_HOST         = \"https://dbc-1b5e869b-0d1a.cloud.databricks.com\"\n$env:DATABRICKS_TOKEN        = \"REDACTED\"\n$env:DATABRICKS_WAREHOUSE_ID = \"9d0fe00fe4756c71\"\nD:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek\\.venv\\Scripts\\devmemory.exe serve\n```\n\nThat's the build with Genie + the config field, and it's what the working end-to-end test used.\n\nIf you also want the **published** package to have Genie, the dev1 upload still needs to run — check the output when you run this (it likely errored):\n\n```powershell\ncd D:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek\npython -m twine upload --username __token__ --password \"REDACTED\" dist/devmemory_cli-0.1.0.dev1-py3-none-any.whl dist/devmemory_cli-0.1.0.dev1.tar.gz\n```"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3381,"cache_read_input_tokens":296594,"output_tokens":1347,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":713},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3381,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1347,"cache_read_input_tokens":296594,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3381},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cen2F3sDaExLSTMNL