{"parentUuid":"59d6efc1-ac3c-41c6-883f-b67e9f51462c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen2je4JXNP8Yw8LHLbN4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That error means `devmemory serve` was started in a shell without the Databricks env vars. The `genie_space_id` is in config, but the host/token come from the environment.\n\n**Fixed** — I created `C:\\Users\\BANU\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\tl-demo\\.env` with all four values. DevMemory auto-loads `.env` from the working directory, so now it just works with no manual `$env:` exports:\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\BANU\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\tl-demo\nD:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek\\.venv\\Scripts\\devmemory.exe serve\n```\n\nI verified it: `/api/genie/status` → `{\"configured\": true, \"space_id\": \"01f1a9dab...\", \"reason\": null}` with a clean shell. Reload the dashboard → **Ask** and the chat is live.\n\n(That `.env` is git-ignored, so it won't be committed. It holds the real token — delete it or rotate the token after the hackathon.)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":308213,"output_tokens":326,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":326,"cache_read_input_tokens":308213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cen2jDQUovw1FfE1xmwb6","type":"assistant","uuid":"019d5969-cdea-40b9-8bad-3f2b73a191ec","timestamp":"2026-09-06T10:30:32.898Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hacka