{"parentUuid":"e16ab70d-10cf-45f3-8853-54d72746711b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen4Pg4nf2PNgUEAoAiuU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The **Databricks AI/BI Genie Conversation API**, via the `databricks-sdk` (`WorkspaceClient.genie` → `GenieAPI`).\n\nIn [adapters/genie.py](src/devmemory/adapters/genie.py):\n\n| our call | REST endpoint underneath |\n|---|---|\n| `w.genie.start_conversation_and_wait(space_id, question)` | `POST /api/2.0/genie/spaces/{space_id}/start-conversation` |\n| `w.genie.create_message_and_wait(space_id, conversation_id, question)` | `POST /api/2.0/genie/spaces/{space_id}/conversations/{conversation_id}/messages` |\n| *(the `_and_wait` polls)* | `GET .../conversations/{id}/messages/{message_id}` until `status=COMPLETED` |\n| `w.genie.get_message_query_result_by_attachment(...)` | `GET .../messages/{message_id}/attachments/{attachment_id}/query-result` |\n\n- **Client/auth**: `WorkspaceClient(host=DATABRICKS_HOST, token=DATABRICKS_TOKEN)` — a PAT. No warehouse ID needed for Genie itself (the space has its own warehouse bound); we still read `DATABRICKS_WAREHOUSE_ID` for the separate `databricks push` sync path.\n- **Space**: `DATABRICKS_GENIE_SPACE_ID` (or `databricks.genie_space_id` in config) — the Genie space you built over `workspace.devmemory.*`.\n- **Response parsing**: each `GenieMessage.attachments[]` carries either a `text` (the explanation) or a `query` (`GenieQueryAttachment` with the generated SQL + `attachment_id`); we fetch rows for the query attachment and return `{text, sql, columns, rows, conversation_id}`."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":311085,"output_tokens":1168,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":528},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephe