{"parentUuid":"91a6d52b-c1d2-40d5-9058-fa812b249518","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen65B2mQmVnJwkoH5efj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_read_input_tokens":314346,"output_tokens":1397,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":691},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1397,"cache_read_input_tokens":314346,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cen653tPqUqpK5EadD8mD","type":"assistant","uuid":"6bd654ab-4251-4de7-bc9b-79e089f31ebe","timestamp":"2026-09-06T11:14:23.648Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
{"parentUuid":"6bd654ab-4251-4de7-bc9b-79e089f31ebe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen65B2mQmVnJwkoH5efj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Entire is not bundled.** The adapter just does `shutil.which(\"entire\")` ([entire.py:430](src/devmemory/adapters/entire.py#L430)) — it's an external CLI the user installs separately, not a Python dependency, not vendored. At runtime `entire.is_installed()` is `False` and everything Entire-related degrades to empty.\n\nDevMemory's data model is **two layers**, and only the second one is Entire:\n\n### Layer 1 — facts (always works, no Entire)\n| source | how |\n|---|---|\n| **Git** | `GitAdapter` shells out to `git` — commits, branches, `diff`, diff stats, changed files, parent SHAs. Every `DevelopmentVersion` is anchored to a real commit. |\n| **Tests** | `TestAdapter` runs your configured test command and parses pytest / jest / go output. |\n| **Metrics** | a `metrics.json` file you maintain in the repo. |\n| **Regressions** | computed by comparing metrics/tests between versions. |\n\nThat's what powers the timeline, comparisons, search, \"previous attempts\" memory, analytics, Databricks sync, and the state-aware loop.\n\n### Layer 2 — checkpoint context (needs Entire)\nAgent name, model, token counts, the AI session + its intent/prompts. Entire captures AI coding sessions and exposes them; DevMemory associates them to commits via a `Entire-Checkpoint:` git trailer or heuristic matching. The `entire graph` plugin additionally gives change-impact analysis.\n\nWithout Entire: `agent`, `model`, `primary_checkpoint`, session/token data are all `null`, and there's no impact graph. You record versions with `devmemory checkpoint --allow-no-entire`.\n\n### Bottom line\nIt's a **git-first tool** — fully usable without Entire, but you lose the \"which agent / which model / what was the AI doing\" narrative that's the main thing separating it from plain `git log` tooling. There's also no automatic session capture without Entire; you'd be running `devmemory checkpoint` manually (or from a git hook) at each commit."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_read_input_tokens":314346,"output_tokens":1397,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":691},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1397,"cache_read_input_tokens":314346,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cen653tPqUqpK5EadD8mD","type":"assistant","uuid":"60df88b5-8675-4af3-b241-a630181b0d53","timestamp":"2026-09-06T11:14:31.635Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
