{"parentUuid":"76c1e703-ba80-4a1e-a9a7-e68394239a0f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>15000000 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1e44d861-715b-4cae-8b5c-cf4dfcedca92","timestamp":"2026-09-06T11:15:09.529Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>15000000 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
{"parentUuid":"1e44d861-715b-4cae-8b5c-cf4dfcedca92","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen69mCCG5LmJxvqH6xQM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1515,"cache_read_input_tokens":315656,"output_tokens":2503,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1704},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1515,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2503,"cache_read_input_tokens":315656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1515},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cen69VHjAFZ2yESuAaPuR","type":"assistant","uuid":"fdc16dac-59b9-4b72-84f6-a532f1345585","timestamp":"2026-09-06T11:15:41.881Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
{"parentUuid":"fdc16dac-59b9-4b72-84f6-a532f1345585","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen69mCCG5LmJxvqH6xQM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. The key realization: **your MCP server is already the agent's interface to DevMemory** — every `get_state` / `refresh_state` / `create_task` / `mark_complete` call is an AI session touching your package. That's exactly the hook point Entire occupies. You can capture it natively.\n\n## What Entire gives you vs. how to get it without Entire\n\n| Entire provides | Native alternative |\n|---|---|\n| AI session boundaries | The task loop already **is** a session — `create_task` opens it, `mark_complete` closes it. Snapshots timestamp every step. |\n| agent + model | MCP clients send `clientInfo` (name/version) on init; FastMCP exposes it. Capture on first tool call per task. |\n| prompt / intent | The task `goal`, the requirements, and each `report_issue` / `set_requirement_status` note. |\n| token counts | Not available client-side — this is the one thing only Entire (or the model API) has. Leave it null. |\n| checkpoint ↔ commit link | You already do this: `link_commit` on every refresh ties commits to the task. |\n| `entire graph` change-impact | Genuinely separate — that's a static-analysis plugin. Keep it optional. |\n\n## Minimal build (native session capture)\n\n1. **`sessions` table** (migration): `id, task_id, client_name, client_version, started_at, ended_at, tool_calls, commits[]`.\n2. **MCP middleware** in [mcp/server.py](src/devmemory/mcp/server.py): on each tool call, upsert a session row for the active task, bump `tool_calls`, record `clientInfo`. ~30 lines.\n3. **`NormalizedState.session`** already has a `StateCheckpoint` slot — populate `agent`/`session_id` from the native session when Entire is absent.\n4. **Optional `post-commit` git hook** (`devmemory hook install`) → runs `devmemory checkpoint --allow-no-entire` so versions record automatically with zero Entire.\n\nResult: install `pip install devmemory-cli`, add the MCP server to your IDE, and you get session tracking + the loop + prompts with **no Entire, no git hook even**. Entire becomes pure enrichment (real token accounting, cross-tool sessions).\n\nThis is ~1–2 hours of real work (migration + middleware + wiring + tests). Want me to build it, or is this a post-hackathon thing?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1515,"cache_read_input_tokens":315656,"output_tokens":2503,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1704},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1515,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2503,"cache_read_input_tokens":315656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1515},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cen69VHjAFZ2yESuAaPuR","type":"assistant","uuid":"d72f1339-01cf-4fb2-8932-9c6806193997","timestamp":"2026-09-06T11:15:53.860Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
