und_money(1.005) == 1.0\"},{\"rank\":4,\"score\":15.0328,\"file_path\":\"pricing/core.py\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":24,\"focus_line\":20,\"snippet_start_line\":20,\"snippet_end_line\":24,\"symbol_start_line\":20,\"symbol_end_line\":22,\"language\":\"Python\",\"kind\":\"function\",\"symbol_id\":\"local/tl-demo:Python:pricing/core.py:function:with_tax\",\"symbol_name\":\"with_tax\",\"qualified_name\":\"with_tax\",\"signature\":\"def with_tax(amount, region)\",\"signals\":[\"same-cont\n=== verify --help ===\nRun a test command and return an adjudicated verdict, not test output\n\nUsage:\n  entire graph verify --test \"<cmd>\" --repo . [--setup \"<cmd>\"] [--record-baseline path | --pre-edit-baseline path] [--max-bytes 2048]\n\nverify runs your test command and reports WHICH TESTS CHANGED rather than what the runner printed: which newly pass, which newly fail, and which were ALREADY failing before the edit (labelled PRE-EXISTING). Raw runner output is never forwarded — ids are, text is not — and id lists cap at 20 with a count.\n\nRecord a baseline on the pristine tree first (--record-baseline), then pass that file as --pre-edit-baseline after editing. Without a baseline the verdict is a state rather than a delta, so a failure that predates the change cannot be labelled as one.\n\nParsers: pytest, jest/vitest, cargo test, go test, phpunit, rspec, minitest, maven/gradle surefire, ctest. An unrecognised format degrades to an exit-code-only verdict and says so.\n\nFlags:\n  --test <cmd>                 The test command to run (required)\n  --repo <path>                Repository to run in (default: current repo)\n  --setup <cmd>                Command run before the tests; its output never contributes test ids\n  --record-baseline <path>     Write the pristine-tree result to this file instead of adjudicating","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c4211bb6-40a9-4916-9d49-53d58e433858","timestamp":"2026-09-06T11:33:40.040Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a8a0b3dc-dc6f-4cc9-b808-1164c19d9042","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
