{"parentUuid":"143f4566-502b-4bcf-b2ef-8dd74e545195","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen9FchVWZacpTMqY4nku","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenRouter provider is built, wired, and tested — but **your key is rejected**. Both my code and a raw `curl` get the same thing:\n\n```\nGET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/auth/key\n→ 401 {\"error\":{\"message\":\"User not found.\",\"code\":401}}\n```\n\n`sk-or-v1-1bb051…d2151` isn't a valid key on OpenRouter's side — revoked, deleted, or the account behind it is gone. Generate a fresh one at **openrouter.ai/keys**, and (if the account is new) add a little credit — the free tier needs an account in good standing.\n\nOnce you have a working key:\n\n```powershell\n# in tl-demo\\.env  (I already added the line — just replace the value)\nOPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-<new-key>\n```\n```jsonc\n// tl-demo\\.devmemory\\config.json  — I reverted this to rules-only; flip it back:\n\"analysis\": { \"providers\": [\"openrouter\", \"rules\"], \"model\": \"anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet\" }\n```\n\nThen `devmemory analyze <version>` and the task-loop requirement evaluator both use it. `devmemory doctor` will show `llm analysis  ok  openrouter`.\n\n**What shipped** ([2d68b5f](.)): `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` recognised, `openrouter` is a first-class provider (OpenAI wire format, base URL `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`, namespaced model ids), default model `openai/gpt-4o-mini` overridable via `analysis.model`. Lint + types + 20 analysis tests green. Not pushed yet — say the word and I'll push `2d68b5f` to `docs/project-details`."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":438417,"output_tokens":605,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input