{"parentUuid":"c712fa87-60aa-44df-b4d5-3fe710f77cdf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cen9wHkaQPsC78VhmgCx2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both keys work. ✅\n\n| key | status |\n|---|---|\n| **Gemini** `AQ.Ab8RN6JCzLf…` | valid — `devmemory analyze v2` just ran a full analysis with `gemini-flash-latest` |\n| **OpenRouter** `sk-or-v1-381f…` | valid, free tier — `minimax/minimax-m3:free` works (`openai/gpt-4o-mini` and most non-`:free` models need credit) |\n\nNote: your old models are gone in this environment — `gemini-2.5-flash`, `gemini-2.0-flash-exp:free`, `llama-3.3-70b:free` all 404. Current picks: **`gemini-flash-latest`** (Gemini), **`minimax/minimax-m3:free`** (OpenRouter free).\n\n**tl-demo is wired up:**\n- `.env` → both keys added\n- `config.json` → `\"analysis\": { \"providers\": [\"gemini\", \"openrouter\", \"rules\"] }` (model unset → each uses its default; Gemini answers first, OpenRouter/rules are fallbacks)\n\nReal output from `devmemory analyze v2`:\n> *risk high — adds a tier parameter to apply_discount but introduces a confirmed 11.9% latency regression (42→47ms)… Reject and profile apply_discount and line_total.*\n\n`devmemory doctor` now shows `llm analysis  ok  gemini`. The task-loop requirement evaluator uses it too now.\n\n**Committed** as `02a0fb9` (amended the earlier OpenRouter commit — default gemini model is now `gemini-flash-latest`). Local only — say push and `e020848 → 02a0fb9` go to `docs/project-details`."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":577,"cache_read_input_tokens":452316,"output_tokens":754,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":175},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":577,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_to