{"parentUuid":"22aac216-fab3-4609-83c2-81da912939a2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeouVF7EAAdWPxxFozmRF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Redesign published across all four screens — same link: **https://claude.ai/code/artifact/64e00eb2-ab9d-4537-a213-681fb0f2c244**\n\n**The A+B system, applied everywhere:**\n- **Newsreader** (serif) carries the page title and the one *hero line* that reads the situation in a sentence — \"Four of six changes landed clean… both regressions sit in `discounts`, same file twice.\" That's the B move.\n- **IBM Plex Sans / Mono** for everything dense — the KPI strip, the version stream table, requirement rows, the impact table. That's the A move.\n- Warm paper (`#faf9f7`), your existing semantic colors (indigo `#4b41d1`, ok `#0e6b4d`, bad `#b31b28`).\n- Cards only for genuinely boxed content (blast radius, git/checkpoint, the Genie answer). Everything else is hairline rules and left-borders. **Status is one ruled line now, not a full-width callout** — the biggest de-clutter.\n\n| Screen | What changed |\n|---|---|\n| **Overview** | Masthead + inline KPI strip → hero line → repeated-failure (left-ruled) → version stream table + feature-health bars + sparkline |\n| **Task detail** | Hero line reads task state · READY as a green ruled line · requirement rows with `COMPLETE` pills · blast-radius / git / issues stacked right · horizontal #1→#2→#3 timeline |\n| **Version detail** | Newsreader intent + hero line · sticky subnav · trace/record split · risk as stacked left-ruled blocks · analysis with the `gemini` provider tag |\n| **Ask** | Chat with the result table + collapsible SQL inline in the Genie answer, suggestion chips below |\n\nNext step when you're ready: I wire this into the actual React app — `theme.css` token changes, the font swap, and the component rewrites, screen by screen."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_read_input_tokens":538015,"output_tokens":1365,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":718},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1365,"cache_read_input_tokens":538015,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeouV984nFAwaoKfg1UW8","type":"assistant","uuid":"58c97a42-6ad3-4fc7-b7e2-e0e4b1b3524c","timestamp":"2026-09-07T10:16:57.820Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
