{"parentUuid":"0609054c-4f21-43cd-80a4-aac1e0054293","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CepFT5czfiX1fHV3ajrNk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X72rTVTupCX1PisZk2NpGk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd D:/Hackathons/TechWeek && git add -A && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nAdd tactile spring motion at the moments that carry meaning\n\nA small, consistent motion vocabulary (lib/motion.tsx) — press-squish,\nentrance pop, a drawn checkmark, staggered \"thinking\" dots — wired into six\nplaces, not sprinkled everywhere:\n\n- Refresh / auto-loop buttons squish on press; Refresh shows a pulsing ring\n  while a state refresh is in flight.\n- The task status banner springs on every transition and, on READY, draws\n  its checkmark in (bouncy) — the payoff moment of the loop.\n- New state snapshots slide in from the right at the top of the timeline\n  (newest-first now, numbered correctly).\n- Requirement pills tick over their label when the status changes.\n- Version rows enter with a light stagger.\n- Genie's \"thinking\" indicator is three spring-bobbing dots.\n\nEverything respects prefers-reduced-motion: <MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\">\nwraps the app and every discretionary bit is gated on useReducedMotion().\nUses motion's LazyMotion + domAnimation + `m` components to keep the runtime\nlean; bundle +~30KB gzipped (localhost-served, no network cost).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit motion work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":666,"cache_read_input_tokens":604063,"output_tokens":637,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":69},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":666,"ephemeral_