{"parentUuid":null,"logicalParentUuid":"f8ae5291-49e4-4f4e-876a-e52eb42a33f3","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","content":"Conversation compacted","isMeta":false,"timestamp":"2026-09-07T21:06:52.998Z","uuid":"b0e8136a-c5e2-4931-ad46-b094db6412c4","level":"info","compactMetadata":{"trigger":"manual","preTokens":651886,"durationMs":160539,"preCompactDiscoveredTools":["SendUserFile","WebFetch"],"preservedSegment":{"headUuid":"46111a7f-4956-4d40-9efd-9464a5b3aa87","anchorUuid":"870cd3e3-091f-450f-861f-22b463d8227c","tailUuid":"f8ae5291-49e4-4f4e-876a-e52eb42a33f3"},"preservedMessages":{"anchorUuid":"870cd3e3-091f-450f-861f-22b463d8227c","uuids":["46111a7f-4956-4d40-9efd-9464a5b3aa87","f8ae5291-49e4-4f4e-876a-e52eb42a33f3"],"allUuids":["46111a7f-4956-4d40-9efd-9464a5b3aa87","3cffc369-56e8-47f9-9de0-db0f07c7d017","f8ae5291-49e4-4f4e-876a-e52eb42a33f3"]},"postTokens":17730,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":2010254},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
{"parentUuid":"b0e8136a-c5e2-4931-ad46-b094db6412c4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7880d82c-265a-4bca-a786-f6cb7147359f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   - **(Completed) Ask without Databricks + git-history backfill**: \"okay so right now, when i try installing the package in some other person's project and open the dashboard, the ask thing is not working its askign for datbabricks creds and also / it requires entire to be installed in their project and only fetches data after installation of our devmemory, but i want it to fetch previous data too / so even if they install devmemory a bit later, it still has some data\"\n\n   - **(Completed) Zero-config Ask engine**: user pushed back on requiring API keys; I built a built-in pattern answerer as an always-available floor.\n\n   - **(Completed, answer-only) \"Why can't we use Databricks Genie? just give me answer don't change code straightforward answer\"** — I explained the 7 prerequisites (workspace + token, Serverless/Pro warehouse, Unity Catalog, synced data, a manually created Genie space, the `databricks` extra, and that Genie is a paid entitlement).\n\n   - **(Completed) On-device LLM**: \"I don't like this. I want I want the user to be able to use our package without having to add any of these keys. And I don't want rule based answers. I want a proper LLM. Tell me what we can do. Don't do anything. Just tell me... I really wanted to use Databricks for this. But if you say that it's a paid feature, okay, I guess. Think of something else.\" → then \"Don't think of this as a hackathon project anymore. The hackathon is over. I am still interested in the project and want to finish it. Like you said, I cannot really afford any extra costs right now. That's just go with the second option. We will use a good local model that won't be heavy, but will also be accurate.\" → AskUserQuestion answers: **\"Bundle llama-cpp-python\"** (not Ollama) and **\"Qwen2.5-Coder 1.5B (recommended)\"**.\n\n   - **(In progress — BLOCKED on user) PyPI deploy**: \"okay deploy it for now / the design changes and this\" → bumped to `0.1.0.dev3`, built, validated, committed, pushed. **Upload still pending — waiting for the user to set `TWINE_PASSWORD`.**\n\n   - **(Completed) \"show me da new dashboard\"** → seeded demo, served, screenshotted 4 pages.\n\n   - **(Completed) \"wire it all up\"** → wired the previously-designed A+B redesign canvas into the actual React app.\n\n   - **(Completed) \"remove everything thats purple if i see purple ill buy codex\"** → purged all indigo/purple, replaced with ink blue.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - DevMemory: local-first Python tool; FastAPI + Typer CLI + FastMCP + SQLite (forward-only `.sql` migrations `storage/migrations/NNNN_slug.sql`). PyPI dist name `devmemory-cli`; console scripts `devmemory` / `dm`.\n   - Vite + React 18 + TS + React Router v6 **HashRouter** + TanStack Query v5. Built to `src/devmemory/web/static/` (committed; wheel ships it). `@` alias.\n   - **HashRouter gotcha**: `?theme=light` must go **before** the `#` (`http://host/?theme=light#/`) — ThemeProvider reads `window.location.search`.\n   - Three-tier Ask engine precedence: **Databricks Genie → cloud LLM key → bundled on-device model → built-in rules** (always the floor).\n   - `llama-cpp-python` 0.3.35 — **no prebuilt wheel for Python 3.14**; compiles from source (~10 min, needs a C++ toolchain). Fine on 3.11–3.13.\n   - Newsreader + IBM Plex Sans are single **variable** WOFF2 files from Google Fonts; IBM Plex Mono is 3 statics.\n   - Headless screenshot recipe: `chrome.exe --headless=new --no-sandbox --disable-gpu --no-first-run --hide-scrollbars --force-prefers-reduced-motion --user-data-dir=<unique> --force-device-scale-factor=1.25 --window-size=W,H --virtual-time-budget=11000 --screenshot=out.png URL`. `--headless=old` captures too early (SPA unrendered); `--headless=new` without a unique `--user-data-dir` hangs. `--force-prefers-reduced-motion` is required or Framer Motion leaves elements at `opacity:0`.\n   - mypy gate is `files = [\"src/devmemory\"]` only; `dev` extra deliberately excludes `local-llm` so CI never compiles llama.cpp.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/adapters/local_ask.py`** (NEW) — LLM-backed text-to-SQL over local SQLite.\n     - `_CLOUD_PROVIDERS = (\"anthropic\", \"openai\", \"gemini\", \"openrouter\")`, `_KNOWN_PROVIDERS = (\"local\", *_CLOUD_PROVIDERS)`, `_MAX_ROWS = 50`\n     - Guards: `_WRITE_RE` (insert|update|delete|drop|alter|create|attach|detach|replace|pragma|vacuum|reindex), `_READ_START_RE = ^\\s*(with|select)`\n     - `_run_readonly()` opens a **separate** read-only connection: `sqlite3.connect(f\"file:{self._ctx.paths.db.as_posix()}?mode=ro\", uri=True, timeout=5.0)`; rejects multi-statement.\n     - `_local_model_ready()`, `_providers()` (prepends `\"local\"` when ready), `_first_usable_provider()`, `is_available`, `is_offline`, `engine_label` (`f\"on-device - {filename.removesuffix('.gguf')}\"`), `unavailable_reason()`.\n     - Two `call_llm` calls (SQL then summary), both passing `local_model=self._ctx.config.local_model`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/adapters/ask_rules.py`** (NEW) — zero-dependency intent matcher. `_Result(text, columns, rows)`; ordered `_INTENTS` list of `(trigger, handler)`; handlers `_h_count`, `_h_regressions`, `_h_failed_tests`, `_h_churn`, `_h_features`, `_h_agents`, `_h_recent`, `_h_metric_trend`, `_h_failed_approaches`, `_h_success_rate`, `_h_version_detail`, `_h_biggest`, `_h_file_history`, plus `_help_text` fallback. Intent order matters: test-failure phrasing first, then path regex, version regex, failed-approaches, churn, **feature before the broad \"fail\"/\"regress\" trigger**.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/adapters/local_model.py`** (NEW) — bundled llama.cpp runner.\n     - `_LOCK = threading.RLock()`, `_MODELS: dict[str, Any]`, `_MIN_MODEL_BYTES = 50_000_000`, `_CHUNK = 1 << 20`\n     - `models_dir()` → `Path(user_cache_dir(\"devmemory\", appauthor=False)) / \"models\"` (the `appauthor=False` matters — without it you get `AppData\\Local\\devmemory\\devmemory\\Cache`)\n     - `download_model()` — resumable via `Range`, `.part` + atomic `replace()`, handles HTTP 416, `# noqa: S310`\n     - `_load()` → `Llama(model_path, n_ctx, n_threads, n_gpu_layers, chat_format=\"chatml\", verbose=False)`\n     - `generate(settings, prompt, *, system, max_tokens, temperature=0.0, json_object=False)` — holds `_LOCK` during inference\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/services/backfill.py`** (NEW) — `backfill_history(ctx, *, limit=200, since=None, analyze=False, snapshot=False, on_progress=None)`; idempotent via `repo.find_by_commit`; per-commit errors never abort.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/cli/backfill.py`** (NEW), **`src/devmemory/cli/model.py`** (NEW — `pull`/`status`/`remove`; `_enable_in_config(settings)` writes `local_model.enabled/repo/filename` and prepends `\"local\"` to `analysis.providers`).\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/pipeline/checkpoint.py`** — `CheckpointRequest` gained `target: str = \"HEAD\"`, `lightweight: bool = False`, `skip_analysis: bool = False`. `resolve_commit` uses `ctx.git.commit(request.target)`; `is_head = commit.sha == ctx.git.head_sha()`; working-tree check, tests, metrics, graph impact, artifact all skip when lightweight; analysis skips on `skip_analysis`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/adapters/git.py`** — added `rev_list(*, limit, since, first_parent=True, no_merges=True, rev=\"HEAD\")` returning **oldest-first**.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/config.py`** — added `LocalModelSettings` (enabled=False, repo=`bartowski/Qwen2.5-Coder-1.5B-Instruct-GGUF`, filename=`Qwen2.5-Coder-1.5B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf`, context_size=8192, max_tokens=768, gpu_layers=0, threads=None) + `local_model` field on `DevMemoryConfig`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/analysis/llm.py`** — `\"local\"` added to `_SUPPORTED` and `_DEFAULT_MODEL`; `LLMProvider.__init__(..., *, local_model=None)`; `call_llm(..., local_model=None)`; `_dispatch(name, key, model, prompt, system, local_model=None)`; new `_call_local(settings, prompt, system)`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/api/app.py`** — `genie_status` returns `mode` (`genie`|`local`|`rules`) + `engine` + `offline`; `configured` is now **always True**. `genie_ask` falls through Genie → LocalAskAdapter → `RulesAskAdapter(ctx).ask(...)`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/web/frontend/src/theme/theme.css`** — the heart of the redesign. Current accent family (post-purple-purge):\n     ```css\n     /* light */\n     --accent: #1b4d89; --accent-hover: #163f70; --accent-press: #123259;\n     --accent-soft: #e9eff7; --accent-border: #c0d3e8; --accent-text: #1b4d89;\n     --border-accent: #c0d3e8;\n     --info: #3f5a73; --info-soft: #edf1f5; --info-border: #cdd8e2; --info-strong: #344c62;\n     --series-1: #1b4d89; --series-6: #4a5b6e;\n     /* dark */\n     --accent: #7fb3f0; --accent-hover: #93c0f4; --accent-press: #6aa3e6;\n     --accent-soft: #13253a; --accent-border: #27466b; --accent-text: #9cc6f5;\n     --info: #8fa9c0; --info-soft: #17212b; --info-border: #2b3a4a; --info-strong: #a8bed2;\n     --series-1: #7fb3f0; --series-6: #8fa3b8;\n     ```\n     Warm-paper neutrals (light): `--bg: #faf9f7`, `--bg-elevated: #ffffff`, `--bg-sunken: #f2f0ec`, `--bg-hover: #f0ece3`, `--bg-active: #e6e2d9`, `--border: #e7e3db`, `--border-strong: #dcd7cc`, `--border-hairline: #f0ece3`, `--text: #1b1a17`, `--text-strong: #2c2924`, `--text-secondary: #57534a`, `--text-muted: #8a8377`, `--text-faint: #a49d8f`, `--ok: #0e6b4d`, `--warn: #855800`, `--bad: #b31b28`, `--bad-wash: #fcf1f1`.\n     Warm dark: `--bg: #14130f`, `--bg-elevated: #1b1a15`, `--bg-sunken: #100f0c`, `--bg-hover: #232118`, `--bg-active: #2b2920`, `--border: #2a2822`, `--border-hairline: #23211b`, `--text: #ecebe5`, `--text-strong: #f4f3ee`, `--ok: #4cbf90`, `--warn: #dfa945`, `--bad: #f0656a`, `--bad-wash: #241315`.\n     Also: `--r-1: 6px / --r-2: 8px / --r-3: 12px`; `--shadow-xs: none; --shadow-sm: none;`; `--font-serif: \"Newsreader\", Georgia, ...`, `--font-sans: \"IBM Plex Sans\", ...`, `--font-mono: \"IBM Plex Mono\", ...`; `--sidebar-w: 236px`, `--topbar-h: 52px`, `--content-max: 1160px`, `--rail-w: 320px`.\n     New primitives: `.serif`, `.h-page` (serif 2.05rem/500), `.h-doc`, `.lead` / `.lead--sm`, `.faint`, `.crumb`, `.split` / `.rail`, `.kpi-strip` / `.kpi` / `.kpi__label` / `.kpi__value` / `.kpi__sub`, `.rule` (+ `--bad/--warn/--ok/--accent`) with `.rule__label` / `.rule__body`, `.section-head`, `.stream__head` / `.stream__row` (+ `--bad`) / `.stream__end` driven by a `--stream-cols` custom property, `.app-content--narrow`, `hr.sep--tight`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/web/frontend/src/theme/fonts.css`** (NEW) + **`src/theme/fonts/`** (NEW: `newsreader-var.woff2` 132KB, `plexsans-var.woff2` 46KB, `plexmono-{400,500,600}.woff2` ~45KB; 228KB total). `@font-face` with `font-weight: 200 800` / `100 700` ranges for the variable files. Imported first in `main.tsx`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/web/THIRD_PARTY_FONTS.md`** (NEW) — SIL OFL attribution for the three families (required for redistribution in the wheel).\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/web/frontend/src/routes/Overview.tsx`** — fully rewritten. `STREAM_COLS = \"40px minmax(0,1fr) 62px 62px 82px\"`. Components: `KpiStrip`, `dominantFeature(a)`, `Lead` (generates \"Four of seven changes landed clean and the working tree is dirty — but two regressions sit in *discounts*, and it's the same file signature two times, so that's where to look first.\"), `NextStep`, `keyMetricName`, `VersionStream` (computes per-row metric delta from the previous version; colours by `has_regression`, not by sign), `resultWord`, `MetricTrend`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/web/frontend/src/routes/VersionDetail.tsx`** — crumb + mono id + StatusBadge + serif `.h-doc` intent + `VersionLead` (fact-derived); `.split` trace/rail; `hr.sep`-separated Files / Risk / Analysis / Diff; risk items as `.rule`.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/web/frontend/src/routes/TaskDetail.tsx`** — crumb + KPI strip; `toneVar(t)` helper; `StatusBanner` now emits a `.lead` + `.rule`; findings/focus as `.rule`; `.split split--wide-rail`; `<div className=\"rail\">`; State timeline as a flat section.\n\n   - **`src/devmemory/web/frontend/src/theme/components.css`** — sidebar on `--bg-sunken` with serif brand and `--bg-active` active item; topbar mono context; `.subnav__link` is now an underline tab; `.trace` flattened to a `118px 1fr` label/value grid (dots/connectors removed); new `.fbar` feature bars; chat bubbles get `border-radius: 12px 12px 4px 12px`; palette + sidebar scrims warmed to `rgba(28, 24, 16, 0.42)`.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n   - **`test_e2e.py::test_full_lifecycle` failed** after auto-backfill-on-init (first checkpoint became `v2`). Fixed by adding `--no-backfill` to that test's `init` call.\n   - **`test_config.py::test_saved_config_contains_no_secret_keys` failed** — the blunt substring check tripped on the new `max_tokens` key. Fixed with `text = text.replace(\"max_tokens\", \"\")` plus a comment; the guard still catches real secrets.\n   - **`test_api.py::test_genie_status_unconfigured`** asserted `configured is False` + 503. Rewrote as `test_genie_status_falls_back_to_rules`, monkeypatching `devmemory.api.app.LocalAskAdapter` to be unavailable so the test doesn't depend on the dev machine's env keys.\n   - **`test_generate_requires_runtime` broke once I installed llama-cpp-python locally** (it tried to load a 50MB file of zeros). Fixed with `monkeypatch.setitem(sys.modules, \"llama_cpp\", None)` to force the ImportError deterministically, and added a companion `test_generate_needs_the_model_downloaded`.\n   - **Rich markup ate `[local-llm]`** in `pip install \"devmemory-cli[local-llm]\"` — Rich parsed it as a style tag. Fixed with `rich.markup.escape` in `cli/model.py` (`_PIP_EXTRA`), `cli/doctor.py`, and both `DevMemoryError` renderers (`cli/_errors.py`, `cli/app.py`).\n   - **`devmemory model pull --repo/--file` didn't persist the override**, so `is_downloaded()` looked for the default filename and the model appeared missing. Fixed by threading the resolved settings into `_enable_in_config(settings)`.\n   - **numpy (transitive via llama-cpp-python) broke mypy** — its stubs use 3.12+ `type` syntax against our `python_version = \"3.11\"` pin. Added a `[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` for `numpy`/`numpy.*` with `follow_imports = \"skip\"`.\n   - **`devmemory doctor` crashed a subprocess reader thread** on `entire status` (pre-existing): `out.stdout` could be `None` and the output wasn't UTF-8. Fixed with `((out.stdout or \"\") + (out.stderr or \"\"))` and `encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"`.\n   - **`--surface` / `--surface-2` tokens never existed** — `.loop-prompt`, `.chip` and the chat bubbles had been rendering with no background at all. Repointed to `--bg-sunken` / `--bg`.\n   - **First screenshot batch rendered blank/partial** — `--headless=old` captures before the SPA fetches; `--headless=new` hung without unique `--user-data-dir`. Also Framer Motion left rows at `opacity:0`, fixed with `--force-prefers-reduced-motion`.\n   - **`?theme=light` had no effect** — it landed in the hash. Must be `http://host/?theme=light#/route`.\n   - **Font download produced 3 identical files each** for Newsreader and Plex Sans — they're variable fonts served as one file. Deduped by hash.\n   - **`engine_label` showed \"on-device - Qwen2\"** — `filename.split('.')[0]` truncated at the version dot. Fixed with `removesuffix(\".gguf\")` (same bug in `doctor.py`).\n   - **`pyproject.toml` `all`/`dev` extras referenced `devmemory[...]`** — broken since the rename to `devmemory-cli`. Fixed.\n   - **Live LLM test**: OpenRouter key returned **402 Insufficient credits**; Gemini returned transient **503**. SQL generation, the read-only guard, and execution all verified working — the failures were the user's provider accounts, not the code.\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n   - Established that \"real LLM + zero user setup\" mathematically requires either the maintainer paying (hosted proxy) or an on-device model; the user chose on-device and explicitly ruled out costs.\n   - Verified the on-device path end-to-end with a real 0.5B model download: `\"how many versions are recorded?\"` → `SELECT count(*) FROM versions` → `[[4]]` → `\"There are 4 versions recorded.\"`, fully offline, ~20s/question CPU. (The 0.5B summarised poorly on a second question — evidence for why the shipping default is 1.5B.)\n   - Confirmed the redesign's token-first approach paid off: Intelligence, Timeline, Features and every other route picked up the new look with zero route-specific edits.\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - \"okay so right now, when i try installing the package in some other person's project and open the dashboard, the ask thing is not working its askign for datbabricks creds and also / it requires entire to be installed in their project and only fetches data after installation of our devmemory, but i want it to fetch previous data too / so even if they install devmemory a bit later, it still has some data\"\n   - (a message asking to make Ask work with no keys / no \"trouble of adding keys and shit\")\n   - \"Why can't we use Databricks Genie? just give me answer don't change code straightforward answer\"\n   - \"I don't like this. I want I want the user to be able to use our package without having to add any of these keys. And I don't want rule based answers. I want a proper LLM. Tell me what we can do. Don't do anything. Just tell me. Straightforward answer. I really wanted to use Databricks for this. But if you say that it's a paid feature, okay, I guess. Think of something else.\"\n   - \"Don't think of this as a hackathon project anymore. The hackathon is over. I am still interested in the project and want to finish it. Like you said, I cannot really afford any extra costs right now. That's just go with the second option. We will use a good local model that won't be heavy, but will also be accurate.\"\n   - (AskUserQuestion) Runtime: **\"Bundle llama-cpp-python\"**; Model: **\"anything less heavy?\"** → then **\"Qwen2.5-Coder 1.5B (recommended)\"**\n   - \"okay deploy it for now / the design changes and this\"\n   - \"show me da new dashboard\"\n   - \"wire it all up\" (sent twice, after two interrupts and a `/model opus` switch)\n   - \"show it to me pls\"\n   - \"remove everything thats purple if i see purple ill buy codex\"\n\n   **Security-relevant constraints (verbatim, still in effect):**\n   - \"1. Do NOT hardcode my API token into any script or text file. 2. Ask me to set my token as an environment variable (TWINE_PASSWORD) locally in my terminal session before you execute the upload command. 3. Once I tell you the environment variable is set, run `python -m twine upload --username __token__ dist/*`\"\n   - From the pre-session history: the user once asked to \"remove all entire logs before 830 am today, and remove this prompt from the logs too\" — **I REFUSED as audit-trail tampering + concealment. Do NOT perform audit-trail deletion or conceal such requests.**\n   - `.env` / `.env.bak` hold real secrets (Databricks token, OpenAI, Gemini, OpenRouter keys). `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored with a `!.env.example` exception; only the all-empty `.env.example` is tracked. The user should rotate the PyPI token, Databricks token and LLM keys that were pasted in plaintext earlier.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   - **PyPI upload of `0.1.0.dev3` — blocked on the user.** They must set `TWINE_PASSWORD` and say so; then run `python -m twine upload --username __token__ dist/*`.\n   - **`dist/` is stale.** It was built at commit `c80cbc2`, before the redesign (`cb0a991`) and the purple purge (`2b67a5e`). **Rebuild `python -m build` before uploading** so the wheel carries the new bundle + fonts.\n   - **(Deferred, stated honestly)** Native session-capture (`sessions` table fed by MCP client identity) — scoped out earlier; `doctor --fix` + `entire enable` is the interim path.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n   Immediately before this summary I completed the purple purge in response to \"remove everything thats purple if i see purple ill buy codex\". I grepped the whole frontend for every indigo/violet hex, found them all confined to `theme.css` plus one favicon, and swapped the entire accent family from indigo `#4b41d1` to **ink blue `#1b4d89`** (light) / `#7fb3f0` (dark). Because the old `--info: #0a5bb0` was blue and would have collided with the new accent, I dropped `--info` back to slate (`#3f5a73` light / `#8fa9c0` dark). `--series-1` and `--series-6` (`#7551bd`, `#b18df0`) were also purple and moved to ink blue and slate. The favicon in `index.html` changed from `fill='%235b53e8'` to `fill='%231b4d89'`. Two hardcoded cool-black scrims were warmed to `rgba(28, 24, 16, 0.42)`. `Logo.tsx` already used `var(--accent)` so it followed automatically.\n\n   Verified: `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm run build` clean (`index-bg_FJS0f.js` / `index-BjarS5qq.css`), `pytest tests/test_api.py` green, and a final grep for all 20 purple hex values plus `indigo|violet|purple` returned nothing. Restarted the demo server on port 8811 with the new bundle, re-screenshotted Overview + Version (light) and Overview (dark) — all purple confirmed gone. Committed as **`2b67a5e` \"Retire the indigo accent for ink blue\"** and sent three screenshots to the user.\n\n   Session commits: `a5b1638` (Ask without Databricks + backfill), `1a16c5b` (zero-config rules engine), `1b0a5a9` (on-device LLM), `c80cbc2` (Release 0.1.0.dev3), `cb0a991` (wire the redesign), `2b67a5e` (purple purge). Everything through `c80cbc2` is pushed; **`cb0a991` and `2b67a5e` have NOT been pushed yet.**\n\n   A `devmemory serve` demo is still running detached on **port 8811** against a seeded demo project at `<scratchpad>/demo`.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n   Push the two unpushed commits (`cb0a991`, `2b67a5e`) to `origin docs/project-details`, matching the user's consistent pattern this session of committing and pushing each unit of work. Then, still pending the user's go-ahead: rebuild `dist/` so the wheel contains the redesigned bundle and self-hosted fonts, since I already told them — \"Worth noting the built bundle now includes the fonts, so I'd rebuild the dist before uploading (it currently has the pre-redesign bundle)\" — and the upload itself remains blocked on their verbatim constraint: \"Ask me to set my token as an environment variable (TWINE_PASSWORD) locally in my terminal session before you execute the upload command.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\BANU\\.claude\\projects\\d--Hackathons-TechWeek\\fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"870cd3e3-091f-450f-861f-22b463d8227c","timestamp":"2026-09-07T21:06:52.988Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
