{"parentUuid":"e6eb5ec9-72ea-41ba-9f17-4196cc9bfa3a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5bbddbb1-bc91-43d1-9778-b85a5f814549","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FxSrtf8mV2j15vHUAGBFnA","type":"tool_result","content":"                 │\n          AI coding agent            ← you keep your editor & agent\n                 │\n          Entire checkpoint          ← why / who / how  (github.com/entireio/cli)\n                 │\n            Git commit               ← what changed, exactly\n                 │\n       tests · metrics · results     ← the outcome\n                 │\n       Development Version  ← DevMemory: the join\n                 │\n     ┌───────────┴───────────┐\n dashboard                 MCP / API\n (a human understands)     (the next agent understands)\n```\n\n## Quickstart\n\n```bash\npython -m venv .venv\n# Windows:  .venv\\Scripts\\activate     POSIX:  source .venv/bin/activate\npip install -e \".[dev]\"          # or:  pip install devmemory\n\ncd your-repo\ndevmemory init --name \"My Project\"\n```\n\n`init` backfills a lightweight Development Version for each of the last 100 commits,\nso an existing project has a populated timeline from the start (`--no-backfill` to\nskip it; `devmemory backfill --limit N --since <date>` to import more later).\n\nThen, after each meaningful AI-assisted commit:\n\n```bash\ndevmemory checkpoint --intent \"what you were trying to do\"\n```\n\nDevMemory finds the Entire checkpoint for the commit (or records without one),\nruns your configured tests and metrics, detects regressions against the previous\nversion, checks whether this area has failed before, generates an analysis\n(kept separate from the facts), and stores one **Development Version**.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5d3d96ae-8053-4b8d-b79d-de56812ae69a","timestamp":"2026-09-07T21:24:35.870Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"                 │\n          AI coding agent            ← you keep your editor & agent\n                 │\n          Entire checkpoint          ← why / who / how  (github.com/entireio/cli)\n                 │\n            Git commit               ← what changed, exactly\n                 │\n       tests · metrics · results     ← the outcome\n                 │\n       Development Version  ← DevMemory: the join\n                 │\n     ┌───────────┴───────────┐\n dashboard                 MCP / API\n (a human understands)     (the next agent understands)\n```\n\n## Quickstart\n\n```bash\npython -m venv .venv\n# Windows:  .venv\\Scripts\\activate     POSIX:  source .venv/bin/activate\npip install -e \".[dev]\"          # or:  pip install devmemory\n\ncd your-repo\ndevmemory init --name \"My Project\"\n```\n\n`init` backfills a lightweight Development Version for each of the last 100 commits,\nso an existing project has a populated timeline from the start (`--no-backfill` to\nskip it; `devmemory backfill --limit N --since <date>` to import more later).\n\nThen, after each meaningful AI-assisted commit:\n\n```bash\ndevmemory checkpoint --intent \"what you were trying to do\"\n```\n\nDevMemory finds the Entire checkpoint for the commit (or records without one),\nruns your configured tests and metrics, detects regressions against the previous\nversion, checks whether this area has failed before, generates an analysis\n(kept separate from the facts), and stores one **Development Version**.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e6eb5ec9-72ea-41ba-9f17-4196cc9bfa3a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
