{"parentUuid":"2c571620-b72f-4cf2-ad7e-a9a599ed85cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CepnTSnL4dRYg1vuJmJC2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011MnzwLfMPPsCKVQN3ebgiK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"d:/Hackathons/TechWeek\" && sed -n '30,42p' docs/STATE_LOOP.md","description":"Check rest of STATE_LOOP block"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1427,"cache_read_input_tokens":82592,"output_tokens":906,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":467},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1427,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":906,"cache_read_input_tokens":82592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1427},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CepnTRs2AWSezmYJmVdJ7","type":"assistant","uuid":"c77f241a-2274-458a-9361-cab65ae9ad75","timestamp":"2026-09-07T21:25:09.594Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
{"parentUuid":"2c571620-b72f-4cf2-ad7e-a9a599ed85cf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5bbddbb1-bc91-43d1-9778-b85a5f814549","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GFJnaeCUtbRoXHJxYiuDHJ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek\\docs\\STATE_LOOP.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b3c36019-8018-4f93-8ee5-df3a3986bfcc","timestamp":"2026-09-07T21:25:09.956Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"d:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek\\docs\\STATE_LOOP.md","oldString":"Any DevMemory project works. Seed the demo, then drive the loop:\n\n```bash\npython examples/demo/seed.py /tmp/devmemory-demo && cd /tmp/devmemory-demo\n\ndevmemory task new \"Add a currency helper to pricing/ and a test for it\" \\\n    --test \"python -m pytest -q\"","newString":"Any DevMemory project works. From a repo you have run `devmemory init` in:\n\n```bash\ndevmemory task new \"Add a currency helper and a test for it\" \\\n    --test \"python -m pytest -q\"","originalFile":"# The state-aware coding loop\n\nA closed feedback loop around an AI coding agent, built on DevMemory's existing\nevidence collectors. The agent implements; the **State Engine** aggregates Git +\nEntire + tests + (optional) graph into one normalized state and an evidence-based\nstatus. See [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) for the agent protocol.\n\n```\nhuman task → normalize into requirements → agent inspects repo → edits code\n   → tests → commit → Entire checkpoint → refresh_state → new state\n   → agent continues (NEEDS_WORK) / stops (READY) / escalates (BLOCKED)\n```\n\n## Try it\n\nAny DevMemory project works. Seed the demo, then drive the loop:\n\n```bash\npython examples/demo/seed.py /tmp/devmemory-demo && cd /tmp/devmemory-demo\n\ndevmemory task new \"Add a currency helper to pricing/ and a test for it\" \\\n    --test \"python -m pytest -q\"\ndevmemory task state                 # the dashboard: NEEDS_WORK, requirements 0/2\n\n# ... agent inspects the repo, implements pricing/currency.py + a test, commits ...\n\ndevmemory task requirement R1 -s complete -m \"added pricing/currency.py\"\ndevmemory task refresh               # re-collects evidence; R2 (tests) verified\ndevmemory task state                 # READY\ndevmemory task history               # snapshot #1 NEEDS_WORK → #2 READY\n```\n\nOver MCP the same flow is `create_task` → `get_state` → *(implement)* →\n`set_requirement_status` → `refresh_state` → read `overall_status`.\n\n## The normalized state\n\n`get_state` / `refresh_state` return a compact object — **not** the repository.\nIt carries: the task + its requirements (each `COMPLETE`/`PARTIAL`/`INCOMPLETE`/\n`UNKNOWN` with a reason), the current/last checkpoint id and session id, the Git\nbranch/SHA/diffstat/tree-clean flag, the test command + pass/fail + status, a\nchange-impact count (`available: false` when the graph plugin is absent),\nunresolved items, findings, `recommended_focus`, and `overall_status`.\n\n## Status\n\n| status | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `IN_PROGRESS` | actively worked on; no completion evaluation yet |\n| `NEEDS_WORK` | a requirement is incomplete, tests fail, or an issue is open |\n| `READY` | requirements satisfied, tests pass, no open issues, tree clean |\n| `BLOCKED` | can't safely continue — human/external decision needed, or git unavailable |\n\n`READY` is evidence-based, not a proof. `mark_complete` runs a full refresh and\nreturns the state; it never blindly marks `READY`.\n\n## What it does not do\n\nNo custom checkpoint store (Entire owns that, git-refs backend), no second git\nbranch, no autonomous background process (the loop is driven by the agent's MCP\ncalls), no repository dump into the state, no fabricated metrics or checkpoint\nids. The engine never edits application code.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":12,"newStart":13,"newLines":10,"lines":[" "," ## Try it"," ","-Any DevMemory project works. Seed the demo, then drive the loop:","+Any DevMemory project works. From a repo you have run `devmemory init` in:"," "," ```bash","-python examples/demo/seed.py /tmp/devmemory-demo && cd /tmp/devmemory-demo","-","-devmemory task new \"Add a currency helper to pricing/ and a test for it\" \\","+devmemory task new \"Add a currency helper and a test for it\" \\","     --test \"python -m pytest -q\""," devmemory task state                 # the dashboard: NEEDS_WORK, requirements 0/2"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2c571620-b72f-4cf2-ad7e-a9a599ed85cf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\Hackathons\\TechWeek","sessionId":"fcec3b82-fe78-4cb6-b1dc-40e4f8a72893","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"docs/project-details","slug":"buzzing-baking-crystal"}
