{"parentUuid":"b6008677-d514-402f-8cbd-e3fb9c542283","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CepoHyTPWZvyTX1JZBteg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TTsHbDCU2MZgpzezopP1dM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"d:/Hackathons/TechWeek\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nRemove the demo project and its vocabulary from the product\n\nThe seeded `pricing` demo existed to rehearse a hackathon walk-through.\nIt is not part of the package anyone installs, and its vocabulary had\nleaked into shipped UI strings — the Ask page suggested asking about\n`quote_latency_ms`, and \"Safe to change?\" hinted at `pricing/core.py`.\nA developer installing this into their own repo would see example data\nthat has nothing to do with them.\n\nDelete `examples/demo/seed.py` and `DEMO.md`, drop them from the sdist\ninclude list and ruff's exclude, and repoint the docs that told people\nto seed a demo at their own initialized repo instead.\n\nThen replace every demo-derived hint with one drawn from the project\nactually being viewed: Ask's opener chips now name a real feature, the\ntop-churn file and the first recorded metric; \"Safe to change?\" seeds\nits placeholders from the same churn list it already renders as pills.\nMemory, Search and `devmemory search --help` describe the *shape* of a\nquery rather than naming invented subjects.\n\nREADME's quickstart now leads with `pip install devmemory-cli` (it said\n`pip install devmemory`, which is not the distribution name) and states\nplainly that there is no sample data.\n\nVerified with the built wheel in a clean venv against a fresh three-\ncommit repo: init backfills its history, the dashboard and API report\nonly that repo's data, and Ask answers with no key configured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit demo removal"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"s